---
source: tests/snapshots.rs
expression: help_for(&args)
---
Charge a card or bank account immediately (POST /v2/transactions).

Use `--capture-method manual` to authorise without capturing.

Usage: flute2 transactions create [OPTIONS] --amount <AMOUNT> --payment-processor-id <PAYMENT_PROCESSOR_ID>

Options:
      --amount <AMOUNT>
          Transaction amount (required). Plain decimal, e.g. `100.00`

      --payment-processor-id <PAYMENT_PROCESSOR_ID>
          Payment processor UUID (required)

      --customer-id <CUSTOMER_ID>
          Customer UUID for vault-linked charges

      --capture-method <CAPTURE_METHOD>
          Capture method: `auto` charges immediately, `manual` authorises for later capture
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, manual]

      --reference-id <REFERENCE_ID>
          Merchant-assigned reference ID for idempotency tracking

      --currency-code <CURRENCY_CODE>
          Currency code, e.g. `USD`

      --card <CARD>
          Card PAN (primary account number), e.g. `4111111111111111`

      --exp <EXP>
          Card expiry in MM/YY or MM/YYYY format, e.g. `12/26`

      --cvv <CVV>
          Card CVV/security code

      --payment-method-id <PAYMENT_METHOD_ID>
          Payment method UUID (stored card or bank account) to charge instead of raw details

      --instrument <INSTRUMENT>
          Which container `--payment-method-id` belongs in: `card` or `ach`
          
          [possible values: card, ach]

      --ach-account-number <ACH_ACCOUNT_NUMBER>
          Bank account number

      --ach-routing-number <ACH_ROUTING_NUMBER>
          Routing number (ABA)

      --ach-account-type <ACH_ACCOUNT_TYPE>
          Account type: `checking` or `savings`
          
          [possible values: checking, savings]

      --ach-account-holder-type <ACH_ACCOUNT_HOLDER_TYPE>
          Account holder type: `business` or `personal`
          
          [possible values: business, personal]

      --ach-tax-id <ACH_TAX_ID>
          Tax ID (optional)

      --sec-code <SEC_CODE>
          ACH SEC code: `web`, `ppd` or `ccd`. Required for ACH
          
          [possible values: web, ppd, ccd]

      --requester-ip <REQUESTER_IP>
          End-customer IP address. Default `127.0.0.1`. Required for ACH
          
          [default: 127.0.0.1]

      --same-day
          Request same-day settlement

      --contact-first-name <FIRST_NAME>
          Contact first name

      --contact-last-name <LAST_NAME>
          Contact last name

      --contact-company <COMPANY_NAME>
          Contact company name

      --contact-email <EMAIL>
          Contact email address

      --contact-phone <MOBILE_PHONE_NUMBER>
          Contact mobile/phone number in E.164 form. Required for new bank details

      --contact-sms-consent
          Record the contact's consent to receive SMS

      --tip-amount <TIP_AMOUNT>
          Tip amount to add to the transaction

      --tip-rate <TIP_RATE>
          Tip rate as a percentage, e.g. `18.5` for 18.5%

      --discount-amount <DISCOUNT_AMOUNT>
          Discount amount to subtract from the transaction

      --discount-rate <DISCOUNT_RATE>
          Discount rate as a percentage, e.g. `10` for 10%

      --surcharge-rate <SURCHARGE_RATE>
          Surcharge rate as a percentage, e.g. `3.5` for 3.5%

      --l2-tax-rate <SALES_TAX_RATE>
          Level-2 sales tax rate as a percentage, 0.01-100

      --l3-invoice <INVOICE_NUMBER>
          Level-3 invoice number

      --l3-po <PURCHASE_ORDER>
          Level-3 purchase order number

      --l3-shipping <SHIPPING_CHARGES>
          Level-3 shipping charges

      --l3-product <PRODUCT>
          Level-3 product line item, as comma-separated `key=value` pairs. Repeat the flag for multiple products.
          
          Keys: `productName`, `productDescription`, `productCode`, `unitPrice`, `measurementUnit`, `quantity`, `taxAmount`, `discountRate`.

      --customer-initiated
          Mark the transaction as initiated by the customer

      --pricing-type <PRICING_TYPE>
          Pricing type: `card` or `cash`
          
          [possible values: card, cash]

      --billing-line1 <LINE1>
          AVS billing street line 1

      --billing-line2 <LINE2>
          AVS billing street line 2

      --billing-city <CITY>
          AVS billing city

      --billing-state <STATE>
          AVS billing state code (e.g. `CO`)

      --billing-postal-code <POSTAL_CODE>
          AVS billing postal / ZIP code

      --billing-country <COUNTRY>
          AVS billing country code (e.g. `US`)

      --shipping-line1 <LINE1>
          Shipping street line 1

      --shipping-line2 <LINE2>
          Shipping street line 2

      --shipping-city <CITY>
          Shipping city

      --shipping-state <STATE>
          Shipping state code (e.g. `CO`)

      --shipping-postal-code <POSTAL_CODE>
          Shipping postal / ZIP code

      --shipping-country <COUNTRY>
          Shipping country code (e.g. `US`)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --profile <PROFILE>
          Active profile (environment). `sandbox` (default) or `production`/`prod`
          
          [env: FLUTE2_PROFILE=]

      --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format: table (default), json, or quiet (id only). When omitted, falls back to the `FLUTE2_OUTPUT` env var, then to the `output` key in ~/.flute2/config.toml, then to `table`
          
          [env: FLUTE2_OUTPUT=]
          [possible values: table, json, quiet]

      --debug
          Print HTTP request/response traces to stderr. Card and bank-account numbers are masked to the last 4 digits; CVV/security codes are removed
